## Project Overview

Ansible automation repository scaffolded via `ansible-init`.

## Repository Structure

```
.
├── ansible.cfg              # Ansible configuration (inventory, roles path, vault, become)
├── requirements.yml         # Required Ansible collections
├── inventory/
│   ├── hosts.yml            # Host definitions
│   └── group_vars/all.yml   # Shared variables for all hosts
├── playbooks/               # Thin wrappers targeting hosts + invoking single roles
├── roles/                   # Ansible roles with standard structure
{% if molecule_enabled %}
├── molecule/                # Molecule test scaffolding
{% endif %}
├── justfile                 # Task runner recipes
├── .envrc                   # direnv configuration for Nix dev shell
└── .omp/                    # OMP agent config (skills, agents, rules, MCP)
```

## Build/Lint/Test Commands

Run these inside the Nix dev shell (`just` recipes wrap these):

```bash
# Install dependencies
just install

# Validate Ansible configuration and inventory
just syntax

# Validate a specific playbook (lint + syntax)
ansible-playbook playbooks/<name>.yml --syntax-check

# REQUIRED before declaring any role/playbook change done
ansible-lint playbooks/<name>.yml          # changed playbook
ansible-lint roles/<name>                  # changed role
ansible-lint                                # whole project (for cross-cutting changes)

{% if molecule_enabled %}
# Run molecule tests
just molecule
{% endif %}
```

### Lint Gate

`ansible-lint` MUST pass (exit 0) before any role or playbook change is considered done. Run it against the narrowest scope that covers the change:

| What changed | Command |
|---|---|
| A playbook | `ansible-lint playbooks/<name>.yml` |
| A role | `ansible-lint roles/<name>` |
| Both / cross-cutting | `ansible-lint` (whole project) |

Warnings are allowed; errors are not. Fix all errors before yielding.

## Ansible Best Practices

### YAML Formatting
- Always start YAML files with document marker: `---`
- Use 2-space indentation (Ansible convention)
- Use sentence case for task names: `name: Update apt cache`
- Use `yes`/`no` for boolean values in most Ansible modules (not `true`/`false`)

### Task Naming
- Use descriptive, sentence-case task names
- Prefix with action: `name: Ensure package is installed` not `name: install package`

### Variable Naming
- Use snake_case: `apt_upgrade`, `timer_name`, `script_args`
- Default variables in `roles/<name>/defaults/main.yml`
- Group variables in `inventory/group_vars/all.yml`
- Avoid shadowing Ansible builtin variables

### Role Structure
- Each role is self-contained with tasks, handlers, templates, files, defaults
- Playbooks are thin wrappers: only `hosts`, `become`, and `roles` keys
- Handler-based changes (restart services) go in handlers, not tasks

### Idempotency
- All tasks must be idempotent - safe to run multiple times
- Use `changed_when`, `check_mode` appropriately
- Prefer `apt: name=package state=present` over shell commands

### Error Handling
- Use `failed_when` to specify what constitutes failure
- Use `ignore_errors: yes` sparingly and with comment explaining why
- Use `changed_when: false` when task should never report changes
- Shell scripts: use `set -euo pipefail` for strict error handling

## MCP Server

This project configures three MCP servers in `.omp/mcp.json`:
- `@ansible/ansible-mcp-server` (ADT/ADE tools): `mcp__ansible_list_available_tools`, `mcp__ansible_content_best_practices`, `mcp__ansible_navigator`, `mcp__ansible_ade_environment_info`, and `mcp__ansible_adt_check_env`. Notice that for syntax checks and linting, CLI commands (`ansible-lint`, `ansible-playbook --syntax-check`, `ansible -m ping`) are REQUIRED.
- `@utensils/mcp-nixos`: `mcp__nix_nix` (query packages, NixOS options, flakes) and `mcp__nix_versions` (package commit history).
- `@mseep/git-mcp-server`: `mcp__git_*` tools for structured Git repository operations.

